# Security rules

- Validate all untrusted input at system boundaries.
- Enforce authorization/ownership server-side for conversations, files, projects, generations and billing resources.
- Use least-privilege provider/API credentials.
- Secrets belong in validated runtime configuration/secret storage, never git or browser bundles.
- Redact secrets, auth headers, cookies, payment data and sensitive user content from logs.
- Add rate limits and concurrency limits independently from financial allowance.
- File uploads require size/type validation and safe object-storage keys.
- Do not trust client-supplied model price, provider cost, plan, allowance or role.
- Admin endpoints require explicit admin authorization, auditing and safe defaults.
- Avoid SSRF/path traversal when later adding web/file/agent tooling.
- Security-sensitive changes require tests for failure/unauthorized paths, not only happy paths.
